      "source": [
        "# Development and Evaluation of a Domain-Specific RAG Chatbot for the National Building Code of the Philippines: A Comparison of Gemma 2B IT and Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "32191be5",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "32191be5"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section 1. **Introduction to the Problem/Task**\n",
        "Large language models are increasingly used to build conversational systems, but they may still produce hallucinated or unsupported answers when asked about domain-specific legal or technical documents. This becomes a serious limitation in regulatory settings such as the National Building Code of the Philippines (NBCP), where users often need exact clauses, measurements, and compliance requirements rather than general explanations. In this project, the task is to develop a chatbot that can answer NBCP-related questions in a way that is both fluent and grounded in the source document.\n",
        "\n",
        "To address this, the project uses a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach. Instead of relying only on the language model’s internal knowledge, the system first retrieves relevant sections from the NBCP and then generates an answer using those retrieved passages as context. This design improves reliability, reduces hallucination, and makes the chatbot more suitable for students, researchers, and other users who need quick access to document-supported answers.\n",
        "\n",
        "The project also compares two language models, Gemma 2B IT and Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, under the same retrieval setup. This allows the study to evaluate not only whether the system can retrieve relevant provisions, but also which model is better at producing accurate, concise, and grounded responses from the retrieved evidence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "756f8053",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "756f8053"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section 2. **Dataset Description**\n",
        "The dataset used in this project is the National Building Code of the Philippines (NBCP) in PDF format, which serves as the chatbot’s main knowledge source. This is a closed-domain dataset, meaning that all answers are expected to come only from the uploaded NBCP document rather than from external websites or open web search. The document contains legal and technical provisions on permits, construction requirements, occupancy, safety, lighting, ventilation, and other building-related regulations, making it suitable for retrieval-grounded question answering.\n",
        "\n",
        "To prepare the dataset for retrieval, the PDF text was extracted page by page and lightly cleaned to remove unnecessary formatting noise. The text was then divided into overlapping chunks using a chunk size of 900 characters and an overlap of 150 characters. This chunking strategy helped preserve context across adjacent clauses and improved the retrieval of provisions that span multiple lines or paragraphs. Each chunk was also associated with metadata such as its source page number.\n",
        "\n",
        "After preprocessing, the chunks were embedded using the SentenceTransformer model all-MiniLM-L6-v2 and stored in a FAISS IndexFlatIP vector store. This allowed the system to perform semantic similarity search between the user query and the NBCP text chunks. Overall, the preprocessing and embedding pipeline transformed the PDF into a searchable knowledge base that supports grounded question answering and evaluati"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "fzwcPguW-kFy",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fzwcPguW-kFy"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Section 3. **Requirements**\n",
        "\n",
        "The proposed NBCP chatbot required a combination of libraries and tools for document preprocessing, embedding generation, similarity-based retrieval, large language model inference, evaluation, and web deployment. The system used Hugging Face Transformers to run the selected instruction-tuned models, SentenceTransformers with all-MiniLM-L6-v2 for embedding generation, and FAISS as the vector database for semantic search. Additional Python utilities such as NumPy, Pandas, regular expressions (re), and PDF processing tools were used for text extraction, cleaning, chunking, metadata handling, and result organization. For deployment, the chatbot interface was developed using Gradio, allowing users to interact with the system through a web-based environment.\n",
        "\n",
        "Requirements used: Hugging Face Transformers; SentenceTransformers (all-MiniLM-L6-v2); FAISS; NumPy; Pandas; regular expressions (re); PDF processing tools; Streamlit or Gradio."
      ]
    },
