        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Section 4. **System Architecture**\n",
        "\n",
        "The proposed chatbot uses a retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) architecture for answering questions about the National Building Code of the Philippines (NBCP). In this system, the NBCP document is first preprocessed into overlapping text chunks, which are converted into embeddings using the SentenceTransformer all-MiniLM-L6-v2 model and stored in a FAISS IndexFlatIP vector store for efficient similarity search. When a user submits a query, the system encodes the query into an embedding, compares it with the stored chunk embeddings, and retrieves the most relevant text segments. These retrieved contexts are then inserted into a prompt template together with the user’s question, and the selected large language model, either Gemma 7B IT or Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, generates the final answer based only on the provided evidence. This pipeline, from query → embedding → similarity search → context injection → answer generation, helps ensure that responses are grounded in the NBCP document and reduces the risk of hallucinated or unsupported answers.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Pipeline**:\n",
        "```\n",
        "NBCP PDF\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "Text Extraction and Cleaning\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "Chunking with Overlap\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "Chunk Embeddings (all-MiniLM-L6-v2)\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "FAISS Vector Store\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "User Query\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "Query Embedding\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "Similarity Search in FAISS\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "Top-k Retrieved Chunks\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "Keyword Filtering / Reranking\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "Selected Context\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "Prompt Template + User Question\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "LLM (Gemma or Qwen)\n",
        "   ↓\n",
        "Final Grounded Answer\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
