      "source": [
        "# 5.6 Hallucination Handling and Failure Case Discussion\n",
        "\n",
        "To reduce hallucinations, the chatbot is constrained to answer using retrieved NBCP context. When the evidence is absent or insufficient, the system uses a fallback response (e.g., “Not specified in the document”). During analysis, failures are categorized as:\n",
        "\n",
        "Retrieval failures: low Recall@K (gold page not retrieved),\n",
        "\n",
        "Context mismatch: low Precision@K (retrieved pages are mostly irrelevant),\n",
        "\n",
        "Generation failures: evidence is retrieved (Recall@K = 1) but the model outputs incomplete, off-topic, or incorrectly grounded answers.\n",
        "\n",
        "This separation supports targeted improvements to chunking, retrieval top-K, gating/reranking, and prompt constraints."
      ]
    },
