    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "Tzn0u1iXszgP",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Tzn0u1iXszgP"
      },
      "source": [
        "This table summarizes the average evaluation performance of Qwen and Gemma across 21 questions. Both models achieve recall@k_mean = 1.0 and precision@k_mean = 0.2, which indicates that the retriever consistently returns at least one relevant chunk within the top-k results, but only around 1 out of 5 retrieved chunks is relevant on average. This suggests that retrieval recall is strong for both models, although the retrieved set remains somewhat noisy. In answer generation, Gemma now performs better overall than Qwen, with a higher token_f1_mean (0.608 vs 0.564), showing better overlap with the ground-truth answers. While Qwen has slightly higher token_precision_mean (0.679 vs 0.640), Gemma achieves higher token_recall_mean (0.596 vs 0.535), meaning Gemma captures more of the expected answer content, even if Qwen is a bit more concise. Gemma also outperforms Qwen on numeric recall (0.905 vs 0.714) and unit recall (0.905 vs 0.762), suggesting that Gemma is more reliable in recovering the required values and measurement units in these regulation-style questions."
      ]
    },
