    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "c8snJpyvo1cj",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c8snJpyvo1cj"
      },
      "source": [
        "This section visualizes the mean performance of Qwen and Gemma across the key evaluation metrics: recall@k, precision@k, token_f1, numeric_recall, and unit_recall. The averaged results show that both models have identical retrieval performance, with recall@k = 1.0 and precision@k = 0.2, confirming that each model consistently retrieves at least one relevant chunk in the top-k results, although the retrieved outputs still contain irrelevant chunks. The main differences appear in answer quality. Gemma achieves a higher token_f1 score (0.608) than Qwen (0.564), indicating better overall alignment with the reference answers. Gemma also performs better in numeric recall (0.905 vs 0.714) and unit recall (0.905 vs 0.762), showing stronger ability to recover correct values and units. Overall, the visualization highlights that while both models perform similarly at the retrieval stage, Gemma shows stronger end-task performance in answer generation and factual extraction."
      ]
    },
