      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "Wj_H4NDmrZxt",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Wj_H4NDmrZxt"
      },
      "source": [
        "This table shows the number of evaluation cases classified as Generation failure or OK for each model, using the rule that answers with token_f1 < 0.30 are counted as generation failures. Gemma records 2 generation failures and 19 OK cases, while Qwen records 3 generation failures and 18 OK cases, with no retrieval failures observed. Overall, this suggests that both models are generally reliable, but Gemma is slightly more stable than Qwen in avoiding low-quality generated answers."
      ]
    },
