      "source": [
        "# 7.9 Model Comparison Summary (Gemma vs. Qwen)\n",
        "Based on the results in Section 7, both Gemma 7B IT and Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct performed under the same retrieval pipeline and achieved identical retrieval metrics, with mean Recall@k = 1.0 and mean Precision@k = 0.2. This means that the retriever consistently returned at least one relevant chunk for every unseen question, but also included additional non-essential chunks. Since retrieval performance was the same for both models, the differences in end-to-end performance mainly came from the answer generation stage.\n",
        "\n",
        "In terms of generated answer quality, Qwen outperformed Gemma. Qwen achieved a higher Token F1 score (0.7469) than Gemma (0.5835), as well as higher token precision (0.7828 vs. 0.5045). Qwen also performed better in numeric recall (0.8571 vs. 0.8095) and unit recall (0.9048 vs. 0.7619), which is especially important for NBCP questions that depend on exact measurements, dimensions, and durations. These results suggest that Qwen produced answers that were more focused, more accurate, and better at preserving critical technical details.\n",
        "\n",
        "The qualitative analysis also showed different failure behaviors between the two models. Qwen tended to fail conservatively by responding with “Not specified in the document” when it could not confidently extract an answer, while Gemma often copied broader text spans or section headings instead of isolating the exact clause requested. Overall, the findings indicate that Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct is the stronger model for the proposed NBCP RAG chatbot because it provides better answer quality, stronger precision, and more reliable handling of code-based information."
      ]
    },
